      "content": "Those NPK numbers are a way to measure a fertilizer's content of nitrogen (N), phosphorus (P), and potassium (K). The numbers represent the percentage of each nutrient in the product. For example, a common NPK ratio is 10-10-10, meaning the fertilizer contains 10% nitrogen, 10% phosphorus, and 10% potassium per pound. Higher numbers, like 20-5-10, indicate more nitrogen and less potassium.",
